# D-UMOUNT-ROOT-DENTRY-STILL-IN-USE-DEFERRED-DIR-DCACHE-SHRINK-RACE, H-DS1: the
# TCP half of the same-build A/B of dshrink_umount_gate, build
# 37897D38118AD5E2FAAC4FC (main tree ~/src/mxfs, 0.90.131),
# tests/umount_dshrink_race_ab.sh, 2/net/mesh/direct on g2d (test31 test32).
# The CAW half is tests/queues/umount_dshrink_race_ab.queue (2/disk/caw/mpath,
# labels dsr*); every completed directory reload queues the deferred shrink on
# either transport, and this half shows the gate on the other one.  Chained
# behind queue fvd, which holds run.sh's 2/net/mesh/direct lock on g2c.  Each
# lap: 3 rounds, the test hold dbg_dshrink_hold_ms=1500 set on node A in both
# arms, the gate 0 (control) or 1 (fix) on node A.
#
# VERDICT RULES (written before the first lap; the CAW half's, unchanged):
#   per lap   the harness's RESULT line: a round REACHES when it shows
#             P-DBG-DSHRINK-HOLD and P-DSHRINK-AT-UMOUNT; control
#             CONTROL-SHOWS-CAUSE when a reached round has 'BUG: Dentry';
#             fix PASS when a round reached and no round has 'BUG: Dentry',
#             'Busy inodes' or another WARNING/BUG/Oops line, every umount
#             and mount returned 0 inside its bound and the cold audit is
#             CLEAN; VACUOUS with no reach; FAIL otherwise.  A FAIL is
#             attributed from the round's captured kernel log before it is
#             counted against the fix.
#   SUPPORTED AND FIXED on this configuration: at least one control lap
#             CONTROL-SHOWS-CAUSE, at least two fix laps PASS, no fix lap
#             FAIL on this mechanism.
#   REFUTED   a reached fix round with 'BUG: Dentry' (the gate closed and the
#             flush done, the reference still there), or a control lap whose
#             BUG names the root while A's P199 line for ino 128 in that round
#             reads dshrink=0 (no shrink busy at the BUG).
#   WEAK      every reached control round without the BUG: the hold does not
#             reproduce the race and the fix laps judge nothing.
#
# Bound per lap, the CAW half's derivation: prep 300 + srcversion reads 2x20
# + findmnt 15 + knob set and readback 20 + 3 rounds x 116 + counters 20 +
# chk_clean with alloc_witness 150 = 893 s.
893 tests/umount_dshrink_race_ab.sh dstc1 0 3 1500 2/net/mesh/direct g2d
893 tests/umount_dshrink_race_ab.sh dstf1 1 3 1500 2/net/mesh/direct g2d
893 tests/umount_dshrink_race_ab.sh dstc2 0 3 1500 2/net/mesh/direct g2d
893 tests/umount_dshrink_race_ab.sh dstf2 1 3 1500 2/net/mesh/direct g2d
893 tests/umount_dshrink_race_ab.sh dstf3 1 3 1500 2/net/mesh/direct g2d
